xnu 0446: give the endpoint's BHI interrupt a DMA landing page

Measured 2026-11-26 with 0445: the ROM leaves BHI_INTVEC at 0xffffffff,
preserving it changes nothing, and BHI_STATUS stays 0x0 for 10000 polls. The
doorbell register keeps the sequence, so the PBL never consumes it.

The QCA6490 donor runs on a kernel with no GIC/ITS path either: it points the
endpoint's MSI capability at a retained landing page in the SMMU-mapped DMA
arena (Iova+0x40) and polls. This driver never programmed the endpoint's MSI,
so the PBL's BHI interrupt had no landing page. Program it to a page inside
the wired image buffer, enable bus mastering before the SOC reset
(pci_set_master precedes ath11k_pci_power_up in Linux), re-arm the MSI after
the reset and log the page around the doorbell. Restore mhi_async_power_up's
BHI_INTVEC=0 write.

